This game has many things wrong with it in my opinion. The leveling is extremely slow, playing it by yourself is extremely boring, It has decent graphics but some zones are hideous (cough cough starting area) while a couple are colorful and vibrant, and the classes are not balanced at all.  It has nice combat but it's nothing special and I feel like there are better mmos out there. It's not a bad game by any means but I feel that it's pretty outdated and there are games that do what it does, but better and with things that make them stand out. Tera is an extremely average mmo, with nothing that makes it stand out. I wouldn't get your hopes up if you were expecting an amazing mmo that is different from the rest of the generic wow clones. I would highly recommend this to someone who is new to the mmo genre and wants to learn the ropes as Tera has a pretty decent tutorial and a really nice player base that will answer any questions you have, happily. One of the better player bases in an mmo, might I add.
TLDR;
Would I recommend it? Yes. If you're new to mmos or looking for something that's pretty basic and casual.

Roguelands is a 2D sidescrolling RPG. The combat, while similar in appearance to games like Terraria and Starbound, offers a layer of depth in the form of weapons with specific limiters. Each of the currently available races start out with a different, distinct weapon: Wanderers have a sword that swings in a typical arc, Centurions with a sword that only jabs forward, and Royalites with a wand that shoots out slightly delayed projectiles, while other weapons are currently obtainable through the game's crafting system. Assumedly, future races will also feature their own special weapons.
The game itself was surprisingly difficult with constant environmental hazards complementing enemies with otherwise simplistic attack patterns forcing us into dangerous situation while leveraging the limitations of our arsenal. There's lots of resources to collect, which is then fed back into crafting tables back at the players' hub.
At the time of writing this it is Build v.0.4.6, and right now the game is VERY "Early Access," with many zones still barren/under construction. From our experience last night, it seems that only a couple of the areas have enemies/resources fully implented, but, if the current content works as a clear indicator for how future zones are going to be designed, I have high hopes for this one.
TL;DR The game's pretty cool but it's early access so don't buy it expecting a 100% finished game. DO buy it if you want to participate in the game's development or if you want to try it now and pick it back up in a year or two.
Also, v0.4.7 is slated to release today at (hopefully) 5 PM EST. (
